!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-template-parameter-spelled-like-an-absorbed-argument-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    Inside a template a parameter's name is read before the schema's, and the shadowing rule classifies what the
    template writes, never what it absorbs. `base`'s `f: pick<T>` applies `pick` to `mode`'s member `T`, so a
    parameter of `t2` spelled `T` would change the type of the field `t2` absorbs: a resolver error at `t2`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
